<title>USA: Shell Odessa plant hit by fire, snuffed quickly.</title>
<headline>Shell Odessa plant hit by fire, snuffed quickly.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shell Oil Co said Friday its 28,300 barrel per day Odessa, Texas, plant was hit by fire on Thursday but was quickly extinguished.</p>
<p>&quot;We had a fire at 11 a.m. yesterday and it was quickly extinguished,&quot; said a Shell spokeswoman, adding the fire occurred in a distillation unit.</p>
<p>The spokeswoman could not yet say if production was cut or how long the unit would be down.</p>
<p>Shell Oil Co is the U.S. unit of Anglo-Dutch major Royal Dutch/Shell Group.</p>
<p>((--Laney Salisbury, New York Energy Desk 1212 859-1631))</p>
